mpany operates through two segments, High-Touch Solutions North America and Endless Assortment. It provides safety, security, material handling and storage equipment, pumps and plumbing equipment, cleaning and maintenance, and metalworking and hand tools. The company also offers technical support and inventory management services. It serves smaller businesses to large corporations, government entities, and other institutions, as well as commercial, healthcare, and manufacturing industries through sales and service representatives, and electronic and ecommerce channels. W.W. Grainger, Inc. was founded in 1927 and is headquartered in Lake Forest, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Donald G. Macpherson | Chairman & CEO | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $812K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $60K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["W.W. Grainger, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $67.4B market cap on $17.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 40% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 31-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 31\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 81% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8056094247330644},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3232295.97},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"W.W. Grainger (GWW) Stock Looks Fully Valued Based On Cash Flow","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-gww/ww-grainger/news/ww-grainger-gww-stock-looks-fully-valued-based-on-cash-flow","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793910214.413,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.862,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GWW Q3 2026 deep dive: data center demand and technology investments drive growth","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/gww/news/earnings-call/gww-q3-2026-deep-dive-data-center-demand-and-technology-investments-drive-growth","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793857255.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"W.W. Grainger Inc (GWW) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Double-Digit Sales Growth, Margin ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/w-w-grainger-inc-gww-231330792.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793834010.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Grainger (GWW) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/grainger-gww-q3-2026-earnings-201406000.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793824768.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Grainger anticipates 2026 adjusted EPS of $47-$48 while projecting 13%-14.5% organic sales growth (NYSE:GWW)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4665285-grainger-anticipates-2026-adjusted-eps-of-47-48-while-