pital of 8.7% by 31pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.30).","It runs a 39% gross margin and converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.18x.","ROE of 46% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.4% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.7x net debt to EBITDA ($585.0M of cash against $2.5B of debt), with interest covered 30.8x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 13.5, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.83)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.6% over 3 years, 8.7% over 5 years and 6.0% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 25% of profits supports about 9.9% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 7.5% a year over five years.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (3.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 6.9% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 6.3%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 77%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (15 sales, net $3.2M sold).","It returns 2.2% a year to shareholders (1.5% in buybacks and 0.7% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 41 consecutive years, raising it 6.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 22,100 employees, each generates about $812K of revenue, 2.2x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 6.8% a year.","That works out to $60K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.2M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 81% above its fair value of $7